      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Mithramycin showed a low CSF:plasma ratio of 0.12 and little brain distribution in monkeys, arguing against meaningful CNS access for that compound.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple direct systemic brain-distribution and CSF-detection studies in rats, mice, and humans support meaningful CNS access, while some similar molecules show poor brain penetration. The mixed evidence and low Morgan similarities lower confidence, but the direct positive CNS exposure evidence is sufficient for a pass prediction.",
